    "created_at": "2016-11-17T07:47:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-17T07:47:36Z",
    "body": "From a users' perspective this seems unintuitive. If I set the volume to 0 and then mute it, why would it not be 0 when I unmute it? I see volume and mute status as two separate things. This is also how other things in real life work. If you mute a TV and unmute it, its volume doesn't change. If the problem is that a video/audio element is being set to 0 volume and muted by default, maybe don't do that?\n",
