    "created_at": "2016-11-17T14:18:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-17T14:18:54Z",
    "body": "It's important to separate two things here:\n1. The behavior of the API, `muted` and `volume`. This is governed by the HTML Standard's algorithms\n2. The behavior of the UI controls presented by the browser. These are entirely at the browser's discretion as to what kind of UI they want to present.\n\nYou seem to be talking about both in your post.\n\nWe almost certainly cannot change the behavior of the API, as that would break expectations of web developers. I don't think we'd want to, either; as @Yay295 says, they are independent APIs.\n\nBrowsers, however, can do whatever they want for their UI controls, and this repository isn't really the place to discuss that. If you'd rather that your favorite browser change their controls' behavior or appearance in some way, you'd best file an issue on that browser.\n",
